/-
# Characteristic quotients of free groups with fewer generators (Kourovka Notebook Problem 17.62)

Kourovka Notebook, Problem 17.62 (J. Conrad): given a free group `Fₙ` and a proper characteristic
subgroup `C`, is it ever possible to generate the quotient `Fₙ/C` by fewer than `n` elements?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Basic
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.Basic
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.QuotientGroup.Defs

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupCharacteristicQuotientRankKourovka17Problem62Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 17.62 (J. Conrad). UnsolvedMath record
UM-00701364 (`KOU-17.62`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The target is the answer in the form given by the resolution: for every `n ≥ 3`, where two
generators are fewer than `n`, there is a proper characteristic subgroup `C` of `Fₙ` with `Fₙ/C`
generated by two elements.
-/

/-- Kourovka 17.62 (J. Conrad), for every rank where it can hold: for every `n ≥ 3` the free group
`Fₙ` has a proper characteristic subgroup `C` such that `Fₙ / C` is generated by two (fewer than
`n`) elements. -/
def characteristicQuotientFewerGenerators : Prop :=
  ∀ n : ℕ, 3 ≤ n → ∃ (C : Subgroup (FreeGroup (Fin n))) (_ : C.Characteristic), C ≠ ⊤ ∧
    ∃ a b : FreeGroup (Fin n) ⧸ C, Subgroup.closure {a, b} = ⊤

/--
Resolved true: Coulon and Fournier-Facio (Theorem 1.1) prove that for all `n ≥ 2` the free group
`Fₙ` admits continuum many pairwise non-isomorphic 2-generated infinite simple characteristic
quotients; for `n ≥ 3` such a quotient `Fₙ/C` is generated by fewer than `n` elements, and `C` is
proper since the quotient is infinite. The Kourovka Notebook (21st issue) answers 17.62 "Yes, it is
possible". Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The
Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 17.62 (J. Conrad); resolution: R.
Coulon and F. Fournier-Facio, Infinite simple characteristic quotients, preprint, arXiv:2312.11684,
Theorem 1.1 (for all n ≥ 2, the free group of rank n admits continuum many pairwise non-isomorphic,
2-generated, infinite, simple, characteristic quotients; Section 1 notes that this answers Problem
17.62); the Kourovka Notebook (21st issue) marks 17.62 solved (Yes, it is possible; moreover, for
all n ≥ 2, F_n admits continuum many pairwise non-isomorphic infinite simple characteristic
2-generated quotients), https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.11684.
-/
public theorem_wanted characteristicQuotientFewerGenerators_holds :
    characteristicQuotientFewerGenerators

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupCharacteristicQuotientRankKourovka17Problem62Wanted
